|ID = 861
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Vornado
|name2 = Tempest King Vornado
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Tempest King Vornado''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
If many of Tempest King Vornado's attributes appear familiar to you, it's because they are. This unit is effectively a damage-oriented [[Hevijak the Wicked (Uber Rare Cat)|Hevijak the Wicked]], exchanging Resistance for [[Massive Damage]] and Knockback for [[Slow]], while targeting the exact same traits.

To cut straight to the point, Vornado is a great nuker for Aku, boasting an expansive [[Long Distance]] effective range that doesn't leave much of a blind spot. This makes matchups against backliners and midrangers like [[Le'Behemoth]]/[[Fallen Bear]] remarkable. It doesn't hamper his performance against annoying melee enemies either. Slow specifically helps with said melees to an even greater extent, locking them in place at a 1/4 uptime after he attacks. His Red target is similarly remarkable. Hitting such a large segment of the battlefield is advantageous in sniping a wide array of enemies like [[Professor A.]] and [[Puffzerker]], knocking them back repeatedly with every attack, thus maximizing his own survivability.

Vornado's damage is about what you would expect from a specialist nuker, dealing 114,750 damage vs. Aku and 153,000 damage vs. Red at Lv.30 (182,250/243,000 at Lv.50). Vornado has phenomenal base HP alongside [[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]], allowing him to take full advantage of his KB count and keeping him quite chilly in the heat of battle, especially when facing Death Surge abusers. He is bound to be an invaluable carry all throughout [[The Aku Realms]] and even beyond!

